course: dictionary
lesson: 13189
title: Frontal: at the front, and straight on
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Frontal means at the front of something, or facing the front. Look for the clue words around it. «The frontal part of the castle was covered in carvings.» The carvings were on the front of the castle, so frontal means front.
explain: Frontal can also describe a bold attack that comes straight at something from the front. «The knights made a frontal attack on the gate.» They charged straight at the gate in the open, not sneaking round the back. Try your meaning in the sentence: does "front" still make sense?
explain: In weather, a frontal system is a line where warm air and cold air meet, and it often brings rain. «The weather map showed a frontal system heading our way, so we packed our raincoats.» The raincoats are the clue. In your body, the frontal bone is your forehead.
fact: Frontal means at the front, or facing the front of something.
fact: A frontal attack comes straight at something from the front, openly and directly.
fact: On a weather map, a frontal system is where warm and cold air meet, often bringing rain.
fact: The frontal bone is the bone of your forehead, and the frontal lobe is the front part of your brain.
fact: In a church, a frontal is a decorated cloth hung over the front of an altar.
exercise: «The frontal part of the castle was covered in carvings.» What does frontal mean here? | Made of gold | *At the front | Underground | At the back
exercise: «The knights made a frontal attack on the gate.» What does frontal suggest about the attack? | Quiet, with no sound at all | Sneaky, from behind the walls | *Straight at the gate, from the front and in the open | Late, after the sun had set
exercise: The weather map shows a frontal system coming. What is most likely to happen? | Snow is falling on the beach | *Rain may be coming | The sun will shine all week | Nothing will change at all
test: Which bone is the frontal bone? | *The bone of your forehead | The bone in your back | The bone in your ear | The bone in your foot
test: «The frontal lobe helps us plan and choose.» What does the frontal lobe do? | *Helps us plan, choose and control ourselves | Digests our food | Pumps blood round the body | Makes our hair grow
exam: Which is a frontal attack? | *A bold charge straight at the enemy from the front | A game of hide and seek | A sneaky raid through the back door | A quiet walk around the castle
